# GitHooks & Pre-Commit

This project makes use of `pre-commit` for quality assurance. If pre-commit changes any files, it is okay to re-add and re-commit. If there are any errors, you should fix them before doing so.

## Useful Commands

```bash
# Test hooks without committing
pre-commit run --all-files

# Biome only (lint/format/safe fixes — same as CI pre-commit hook)
pre-commit run biome-check --all-files

# Prettier only (YAML, HTML, SCSS per .pre-commit-config.yaml)
pre-commit run prettier --all-files

# Biome + Prettier together (typical pass before commit for web/JS stacks)
pre-commit run biome-check prettier --all-files

# Commit without running a hook
SKIP=<hook-id> git commit
```

## Biome (`biome-check`)

When fixing or checking JavaScript/TypeScript/CSS for this repo, **run Biome the same way pre-commit does** so results match CI:

```bash
pre-commit run biome-check --all-files
```

If it fails, **fix the reported issues** (or adjust `biome.json` when a rule is intentionally relaxed for a path) and re-run until the hook exits successfully. Do not only run `npx biome` or a different Biome version unless you are debugging; the hook pins `@biomejs/biome` via `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.

When checking formatting broadly, **run Biome and Prettier via pre-commit** so both match CI:

```bash
pre-commit run biome-check prettier --all-files
```

## Prettier (`prettier`)

Pre-commit runs Prettier on **YAML, HTML, and SCSS** (`types_or` in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`), with excludes for large or generated trees. **Invoke it the same way CI does:**

```bash
pre-commit run prettier --all-files
```

If it fails or rewrites files, **fix or accept the diff**, re-stage, and re-run until the hook passes. Prefer this over ad-hoc `npx prettier` so the Prettier version matches the hook’s `additional_dependencies`.

## Hook Categories

The pre-commit configuration includes several categories of hooks:

- Security Tools
- Code Quality Tools
- Filesystem tools
- Git quality
- Tests
